{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And YHWH visited.</b> Abraham prayed on behalf of Abimelech, and YHWH visited Sarah, as it says: וַה' שָׁב אֶת שְׁבוּת אִיּוֹב בְּהִתְפַּלְלוֹ בְּעַד רֵעֵהוּ (Job 42:10)." "<b>As He said.</b> In His saying וּבֵרַכְתִּי אוֹתָהּ (Genesis 17:16) — and this was that He removed from her the curse of Eve in conception, in childbirth, and in rearing, as it says: הַרְבָּה אַרְבֶּה עִצְּבוֹנֵךְ וְהֵרֹנֵךְ (Genesis 3:16)." "<b>And YHWH did for Sarah as He had spoken.</b> As it says (Genesis 17:16): וְגַם נָתַתִּי מִמֶּנָּה לְךָ בֵּן — not after the manner of those who give birth in old age, who bear mostly daughters."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:30:58.595043346Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}